  "id": "COMPOUND:21079 - PROTEIN:5953",
  "verbalization": "Palmarumycin CP18 is implicated in the regulation of Ubiquitin carboxyl-terminal hydrolase 8 (UCH8) through multiple pathways. The evidence suggests that palmarumycin CP18 acts as a target for a compound that inhibits P2X purinoceptors, which in turn targets UCH8. This indicates a potential mechanism where the compound modulates P2X receptor activity, leading to the inhibition of UCH8. Additionally, palmarumycin CP18 is also shown to target LOUCY, which is itself a target of the same compound and also targets UCH8. This suggests that the compound may exert its effect through a common pathway, possibly by modulating the activity of a shared intermediate, which then leads to the inhibition of UCH8. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between palmarumycin CP18 and UCH8, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
